  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Evidence Room",
    "overview": "The admin UI is a lab bench where every decision the agent makes sits as an exhibit: tagged with an ID, sealed when a human must authorize it, and its chain of custody one click away. A blue-grey bench ground holds white evidence panels; a deep ink-navy rail runs down the left. Colour is not decoration here, it is apparatus: three inks are reserved for three meanings (exhibit yellow, seal red, agent violet) and everything else stays in the neutral blue-grey family, so a newcomer at 3 a.m. can read what matters from colour alone.\n\nDensity is operational, not airy: 15px body, tabular numerals everywhere, tables and custody rows packed for scanning. State is carried twice, in hue and in line form, so it survives colour blindness, dark mode and greyscale: confirmed is a solid line, proposed is dashed (or wireframe in 3D), did-not-run is struck through. The dark theme is a graphite lightbox that keeps the same tag, seal and violet reservations, with each ink lifted for contrast.\n\nThe system rejects the category default of KPI tiles over a grey card grid with one blue accent. It also runs under a strict CSP and fully offline: one self-hosted variable face, a vendored 3D library, an inline SVG sprite, no inline styles or scripts.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Reserved inks: yellow means evidence, red means seal, violet means the agent's own path.",
      "State in line form: solid confirmed, dashed proposed, struck did-not-run.",
      "Full borders and tints for state; never a coloured side stripe.",
      "Notched monospace exhibit tags; custody steps numbered in violet rings.",
      "One variable sans (Public Sans 100\u2013900) plus the platform monospace.",
      "Light and dark follow the OS; both are first-class."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Three Inks Rule",
        "body": "Yellow is only on exhibit tags, red only on seals (approvals, P1, failures), violet only on the agent's own path and decisions. If an element is none of those, it may not use those inks.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Slate Chrome Rule",
        "body": "Every hover, focus, selection and active indicator uses select. Interaction never borrows a reserved ink.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Twice-Said Rule",
        "body": "Every state carries a line-form or text cue as well as a hue: solid, dashed, struck, or a word.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Copyable Mono Rule",
        "body": "Monospace marks identifiers and measurements only; it never sets prose or headings.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sentence Case Rule",
        "body": "Labels, group names and table heads are sentence case at normal tracking; no uppercase tracked labels.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Lift Rule",
        "body": "There is one shadow token; nothing invents a second elevation level.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep yellow, red and violet to their single meanings (The Three Inks Rule); use select for every hover, focus and selection.",
      "Do say state twice: solid confirmed, dashed (or wireframe) proposed, struck did-not-run, plus a word.",
      "Do cite evidence with the notched exhibit tag in front of the claim it supports; leave speculation untagged in a dashed frame.",
      "Do read theme colours from CSS custom properties in JS, and set dynamic geometry through CSS custom properties via the CSSOM.",
      "Do vendor everything: fonts in static/fonts, libraries in static/vendor, icons in the inline SVG sprite.",
      "Do design both themes; the dark graphite lightbox keeps the same reservations."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use a coloured side stripe (border-left accent) on cards, rows or alerts; use a full border and a tint.",
      "Don't write inline style attributes or inline scripts; the CSP (script-src 'self'; style-src 'self') rejects them.",
      "Don't load anything from a CDN or external font service; the product must run offline.",
      "Don't show state by fading alone; fades are for dimming the unselected, not for meaning proposed.",
      "Don't build KPI tiles over a grey card grid with one blue accent.",
      "Don't use uppercase tracked labels or eyebrow text above headings."
    ]
